<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Deliberately a near-empty partial plist.

	     GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE stays YES, so everything else in the bundle's
	     Info.plist still comes from the INFOPLIST_KEY_ build settings and from
	     Xcode's own generation (UILaunchScreen, UIApplicationSceneManifest).
	     This file is the base that generation merges into, and it carries only
	     keys that no build setting can express.

	     Today that is exactly one. BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers must be
	     an array of strings; INFOPLIST_KEY_ values are strings, and Xcode widens
	     one to an array only for keys it knows (UIBackgroundModes,
	     LSApplicationQueriesSchemes). This key is not one of those, so declaring
	     it as INFOPLIST_KEY_BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers silently never
	     reached the bundle at all: BGTaskScheduler rejected registration at
	     every launch and background flight monitoring never ran.

	     Add a key here only when the same is true of it. Anything expressible as
	     INFOPLIST_KEY_ belongs in the build settings, where Xcode keeps it in
	     sync with the target. After every CI build, preflight verifies against
	     the built bundle that the merge happened: that this key arrives as an
	     array, and that the generated keys survived alongside it. -->
	<key>BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>com.jetsetter.pro.disruption.poll</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
